#
# Rear camera video: the EIS algorithm in bypass.
#
# Aperture asks for video stabilization (control.videoStabilizationMode 1) and
# the rear camera has it, so the MediaTek pipeline reconfigures the 1080p
# stream through EIS (eis_mode 0x160, factor 116) and the WPE warp engine.
# On 24.0 every frame recorded that way came out as one flat colour -- in a
# five second clip, luma minimum equal to maximum on every frame but the first
# -- while the front camera, which has no EIS, recorded normally. No error
# anywhere in the camera HAL.
#
# With the algorithm in bypass the same 1080p recording is a normal video, so
# the fault is in what the algorithm computes -- and it has nothing to compute
# from: this phone has no gyroscope (the sensor list is accelerometer,
# magnetometer, orientation, light and proximity), yet the HAL advertises
# video stabilization. Nothing is lost: there was no stabilization to have.
on post-fs-data
    setprop vendor.debug.camera.eis.bypass 1
